<title>USA: CME 1996 volume slips 2.5 percent from 1995.</title>
<headline>CME 1996 volume slips 2.5 percent from 1995.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said volume in 1996 totaled 198,000,759 contracts, down 2.5 percent from 203,153,100 contracts traded during 1995.</p>
<p>December volume totaled 15,429,536 contracts, up 4.0 percent from the year-ago monthly level of 14,829,781 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 5,361,113, up 2.0 percent from 5,254,374 at the end of December last year.  </p>
<p>Major categories were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Dec 1996	% change	 Dec 1995</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   6,411,912	  - 8.0	   6,965,755</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   529,066	   +6.8	     495,229</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   481,963	  +30.2	     370,287</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    451,789	  +56.3	     289,039</p>
<p>  British pound	  326,290	   -2.6	     334,952</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	   263,917	  +51.2	     174,511</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		1,941,367	  +12.5	   1,725,350</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    313,210	  +28.3	     244,214</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 154,623	  +12.8	     137,034</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   1,840,695	   -8.5	   2,011,584</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve     692,340	 +288.6	     178,147</p>
<p>  British pound	   81,800	  -69.2	     266,012</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   188,002	   +2.8	     182,953</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   175,878	   +2.3	     171,849</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  568,259	   -0.1	     568,813</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     60,095	  +35.8		44,256</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.  </p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for December 1996 totaled 12,388,659 and full-year volume stood at 177,027,583.</p>
